     "text": "Johnson Thomas and Stephens Clinic\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI am writing to provide a comprehensive summary of my consultation with Cathy Flores, who presented for a medication refill on October 17, 2024.\n\n**Patient Information:**\n- Name: Cathy Flores\n- Date of Birth: July 31, 1964\n- Sex: Female\n\n**Presenting Concerns:**\nCathy visited our clinic for a routine medication refill. She has a history of an Abnormal pap smear with Cervical Intraepithelial Neoplasia (CIN), which is currently under control with no ongoing medication. she has a controlled seasonal allergy for which she is taking montelukast 10 mg and cetirizine 10 mg daily.\n\n**Vital Signs on Visit:**\n- Blood Pressure: 128/92 mmHg\n- Weight: 184 lbs\n\n**History and Physical Examination:**\nCathy’s vital signs were within normal limits for her age and height. The rest of her physical examination was unremarkable with no acute distress noted. She reported no significant complaints apart from her known conditions.\n\n**Current Medications:**\n- Montelukast 10 mg daily: Cathy has been on this medication for her seasonal allergies, which she reports controlling effectively.\n- Cetirizine 10 mg daily: She also uses cetirizine to her allergy symptoms.\n\n**Medical History:**\n- **Abnormal Pap Smear/CIN:** Cathy was diagnosed with an Abnormal pap smear and CIN in 2009. Fortunately, her condition is currently controlled, and she does not require any additional medication for this condition.\n- **Seasonal Allergy:** Cathy has been managing her seasonal allergies since January 12, 2012, and reports that her current medications are effective in controlling her symptoms.\n\n**Social History:**\n- **Tobacco Use:** Cathy is a former smoker who used to smoke one pack per day. started smoking on June 23, 1996, and successfully quit on February 23, 2025.\n\n**Family History:**\n- Cathy’s mother had a myocardial infarction (MI) at the age of 67. Unfortunately, her mother did not survive the event.\n\n**Conclusion and Recommendations:**\nBased on our discussion and examination, Cathy’s Abnormal pap smear with CIN remains under control, and her seasonal allergies are well managed with her current medications. I recommend continuing her current regimen of montelukast 10 mg and cetirizine 10 mg daily. I will keep monitoring her conditions and adjust the treatment plan as necessary.\n\nThank you for referring Cathy to our clinic. Please do not hesitate to reach out if you require any further information or if there are any changes in her condition.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Melissa Nicholson\nFamily Medicine\nJohnson Thomas and Stephen"
